.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 23, 2026
.Dt EFIBOOTMGR 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm efibootmgr
.Nd show and change the firmware's boot entries
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Nm
.Fl a | Fl A | Fl B
.Fl b Ar bootnum
.Nm
.Fl c Fl l Ar loader
.Op Fl aDv
.Op Fl b Ar bootnum
.Op Fl L Ar label
.Nm
.Fl E
.Op Fl d | Fl p
.Nm
.Fl f | Fl F
.Nm
.Fl n Fl b Ar bootnum
.Nm
.Fl N
.Nm
.Fl o Ar bootorder
.Nm
.Fl t Ar timeout
.Nm
.Fl T
.Nm
.Fl u Ar unix-path
.Sh DESCRIPTION
UEFI firmware boots what its boot entries name: each a
.Li Boot Ns Ar XXXX
variable holding a label, a device path (a partition and a file on it) and
whether it is active, tried in the order the
.Li BootOrder
variable gives.
.Nm
shows and changes them through
.Xr efi 4 ,
with FreeBSD's options and output.
With no option it shows
.Li BootNext ,
.Li BootCurrent
(the entry the system booted from),
.Li Timeout ,
.Li BootOrder
and each entry in it:
.Ql +
marks the current one and
.Ql *
an active one.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-b bootnum"
.It Fl v , Fl Fl verbose
Also show each entry's device path and, if its partition is on this machine,
its device and where its file is here; and the entries
.Li BootOrder
leaves out.
.It Fl a , Fl Fl activate
Make the entry active (with
.Fl c ,
the new one).
.It Fl A , Fl Fl deactivate
Make it inactive: the firmware skips it.
.It Fl B , Fl Fl delete
Delete it, from
.Li BootOrder
and
.Li BootNext
too.
.It Fl b Ar bootnum , Fl Fl bootnum Ar bootnum
The entry, by its number in hex
.Pq Li 0009 , Li Boot0009 .
With
.Fl c ,
the number for the new one, which must be free.
.It Fl c , Fl Fl create
Make an entry for
.Ar loader ,
a file on a mounted EFI system partition, first in
.Li BootOrder ;
inactive unless
.Fl a .
Its device path is built from the partition's GPT entry (number, start, size
and GUID) and the file's path on it.
.It Fl D , Fl Fl dry-run
Show the entry
.Fl c
would make, and make nothing.
.It Fl E , Fl Fl esp
Show the device of the EFI system partition the system booted from; with
.Fl d ,
its device path instead; with
.Fl p ,
where it is mounted.
.It Fl f , Fl Fl fw-ui
Ask the firmware to stop in its setup screens at the next boot.
.It Fl F , Fl Fl no-fw-ui
Take that back.
.It Fl l Ar loader , Fl Fl loader Ar loader
The loader for
.Fl c .
.It Fl L Ar label , Fl Fl label Ar label
The new entry's label; the loader's file name by default.
.It Fl n , Fl Fl bootnext
Boot the entry next time only
.Pq Li BootNext ,
active or not.
.It Fl N , Fl Fl delete-bootnext
Delete
.Li BootNext .
.It Fl o Ar bootorder , Fl Fl bootorder Ar bootorder
Set
.Li BootOrder
to these entries, comma-separated, in hex.
.It Fl t Ar timeout , Fl Fl set-timeout Ar timeout
The firmware's boot menu waits
.Ar timeout
seconds.
.It Fl T , Fl Fl del-timeout
Delete
.Li Timeout .
.It Fl u Ar unix-path , Fl Fl efidev Ar unix-path
Show the device path of
.Ar unix-path ,
a file on a mounted EFI system partition.
.El
.Pp
Changing entries is root's.
FreeBSD's
.Fl k
and
.Fl e ,
a kernel and environment for FreeBSD's own loader, have no use with Limine
and are refused.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 otherwise.
.Sh EXAMPLES
An entry for OxideBSD's Limine, active and first:
.Dl efibootmgr -a -c -l /boot/efi/EFI/OxideBSD/BOOTX64.EFI -L OxideBSD
.Pp
Boot entry 3 next time only:
.Dl efibootmgr -n -b 3
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr efi 4 ,
.Xr efivar 8 ,
.Xr installer 8
.Sh HISTORY
An
.Nm
first appeared in FreeBSD 11.1; OxideBSD's in OxideBSD 0.3.
